
{
  "info": {
    "name": "Kafka Showcase - Order & Inventory System",
    "_postman_id": "kafka-showcase-collection-001",
    "description": "Production-grade Kafka showcase demonstrating:\n- Consistency (partition keying)\n- Throughput (batching & compression)\n- Fault Tolerance (manual offset commit)\n\nRedpanda Cluster: 3 brokers\nServices: Order Service (Producer) + Inventory Service (Consumer)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Order Service",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check - Order Service",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Service is healthy\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"healthy\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Brokers are connected\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.brokers).to.be.greaterThan(0);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_service_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{order_service_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if Order Service is healthy and can connect to Kafka brokers.\n\n**Expected Response:**\n``````"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Order - Laptop",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 202 Accepted\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Order ID is returned\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.order_id).to.exist;",
                  "    pm.environment.set(\"last_order_id\", jsonData.order_id);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Status is accepted\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql(\"accepted\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response time is less than 200ms\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"product_id\": \"prd_laptop_001\",\n  \"quantity\": 2\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_service_url}}/orders",
              "host": ["{{order_service_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new order for a laptop.\n\n**Request:**\n- `user_id`: Customer identifier\n- `product_id`: Product SKU\n- `quantity`: Number of units\n\n**Key Pattern:**\nOrder ID is used as Kafka partition key to ensure:\n- Same order → same partition → same consumer\n- Zero race conditions\n\n**Expected Response:**\n``````"
          },
          "response": []
        },
