    {
      "name": "Load Testing Scenarios",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Bulk Orders - 10 Laptops",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Generate random user ID for load testing",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"user_id\", \"usr_\" + Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 202\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response time < 200ms\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(200);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"product_id\": \"prd_laptop_001\",\n  \"quantity\": 10\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_service_url}}/orders",
              "host": ["{{order_service_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders"]
            },
            "description": "**Load Testing Scenario:**\nCreate bulk order to test throughput.\n\n**Test Metrics:**\n- P50 latency: <50ms\n- P99 latency: <150ms\n- Throughput: 1000+ req/sec\n\n**Run with Collection Runner:**\n1. Select this folder\n2. Set iterations: 100\n3. Set delay: 0ms\n4. Click Run"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Random Product Order",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Random product selection for load testing",
                  "const products = [",
                  "    \"prd_laptop_001\",",
                  "    \"prd_mouse_002\",",
                  "    \"prd_keyboard_003\",",
                  "    \"prd_monitor_004\"",
                  "];",
                  "",
                  "const randomProduct = products[Math.floor(Math.random() * products.length)];",
                  "const randomQuantity = Math.floor(Math.random() * 5) + 1;",
                  "const randomUser = \"usr_\" + Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000);",
                  "",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"random_product\", randomProduct);",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"random_quantity\", randomQuantity);",
                  "pm.environment.set(\"user_id\", randomUser);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 202\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(202);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"product_id\": \"{{random_product}}\",\n  \"quantity\": {{random_quantity}}\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{order_service_url}}/orders",
              "host": ["{{order_service_url}}"],
              "path": ["orders"]
            },
            "description": "**Random Load Testing:**\nSimulates realistic traffic with:\n- Random users\n- Random products\n- Random quantities (1-5)\n\n**Use Case:**\nTest partition distribution and consumer load balancing."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Load testing scenarios for performance benchmarking.\n\n**Run with:**\n- Postman Collection Runner (100-1000 iterations)\n- Newman CLI\n- k6 (recommended for heavy load)"
    },
